  "config": {
    "paper_title": "JEPA-Reg: Predictive Representation Regularization Improves Robustness to Adversarial Lexical Overlap in Paraphrase Detection",
    "paper_claim": "JEPA-style EMA predictive auxiliary loss regularizes the projection space of BERT, creating an inductive bias toward structurally-grounded semantic representations. This improves robustness on datasets where lexical overlap is a misleading surface cue (PAWS, HANS), while requiring no negative pair sampling. Stop-gradient is applied to the TARGET encoder only (consistent with I-JEPA design).",
